## Overview

The checkout flow is in :ref[fig-checkout], the limits are in :ref[tbl-limits] and the client call is :ref[lst-client].
A reference may come before its figure: :ref[fig-states] is further down.

:::figure{#fig-checkout} Checkout flow, from cart to **confirmation**
```mermaid
flowchart LR
  Cart --> Payment --> Confirmation
```
:::

## Limits

:::figure{#tbl-limits kind=table} Rate limits per plan

| Plan | Requests per minute |
| ---- | ------------------: |
| Free |                  60 |
| Team |                 600 |

:::

:::figure{#lst-client title="Creating an order with the client" kind=listing}
```ts
const order = await client.orders.create({ sku: 'A-1', quantity: 2 });
```
:::

## Without an id or caption

A figure without an id is still numbered, but cannot be referenced.

